      "date": "2026-08-10T19:33:54.000Z",
      "content": "Eyes to the skies \u2013 we\u2019re preparing to capture the upcoming solar eclipse in a way only NASA can.\n\nOn August 9, our WB-57 high-altitude aircraft took off from Ellington Field in preparation to capture the Moon covering the Sun on August 12. The team will take off from Iceland and fly in the path of the eclipse, sending back views for researchers to learn more about the celestial event.\n\nTo learn more about the upcoming solar eclipse, visit https://science.nasa.gov/eclipses/future-eclipses/total-solar-eclipse-on-august-12-2026/",
